  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of the 'Stops'. If you know a card is in the dummy hand (because the sequence ended early), you can lead into that suit safely, knowing you will likely hold the last playable card and get to start the next sequence.\n\nSuit Control: If you have a 'Money Card' (e.g., Ace of Hearts), try to maneuver the game into Hearts. If the current sequence is Spades, wait for a Stop, then lead your lowest Heart to move toward your payout card.\n\nThe Dealer's Gamble: As the dealer, you can choose to swap your hand for the 'Dummy' hand. Only do this if your current hand is poor and has zero Money Cards. The Dummy hand is a total unknown but holds the potential for better payouts.",
    Player: "Keep track of the 'Stops'. If you know a card is in the dummy hand (because the sequence ended early), you can lead into that suit safely, knowing you will likely hold the last playable card and get to start the next sequence.\n\nSuit Control: If you have a 'Money Card' (e.g., Ace of Hearts), try to maneuver the game into Hearts. If the current sequence is Spades, wait for a Stop, then lead your lowest Heart to move toward your payout card.\n\nThe Dealer's Gamble: As the dealer, you can choose to swap your hand for the 'Dummy' hand. Only do this if your current hand is poor and has zero Money Cards. The Dummy hand is a total unknown but holds the potential for better payouts.",
