    basic: "Keep track of the 'Stops'. If you know a card is in the dummy hand (because the sequence ended early), you can lead into that suit safely, knowing you will likely hold the last playable card and get to start the next sequence.",
    intermediate: "Suit Control: If you have a 'Money Card' (e.g., Ace of Hearts), try to maneuver the game into Hearts. If the current sequence is Spades, wait for a Stop, then lead your lowest Heart to move toward your payout card.",
    advanced: "The Dealer's Gamble: As the dealer, you can choose to swap your hand for the 'Dummy' hand. Only do this if your current hand is poor and has zero Money Cards. The Dummy hand is a total unknown but holds the potential for better payouts.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't lead your Money Cards immediately. If you lead an Ace of Hearts, you might get the payout, but you also end that suit's sequence instantly.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Watch what other players 'Stop' on. It tells you exactly what is missing in the Dummy hand.",
